1,2$ Hyphae and hymenial elements clamped.
1,0$. Hyphae and hymenial elements clampless, basidia 2-spored:$2-spored form of M. urania

2,3 $ Basidia 4-spored.
2,0 $ Basidia 2-spored: $ M. caesiolivida and 2-spored form of M. filopes
3,0 $ Pileus white to whitish, greyish brown at the centre. Lamellae white. Spores 6.3-7.0 µm long:  $ M. pseudolaevigata
3,4 $ Pileus either not white or, if whitish, spores longer than 8 µm.
4,0 $ Lamellae violet-blue when young: $ M. urania
4,5 $ Lamellae white, yellowish or pale brownish.
5,6 $ Cheilocystidia generally distinctly stalked.
5,0 $ Cheilocystidia short-stalked or (the majority) sessile: $ M. filopes
6,0 $ Odour of iodoform when drying: $ M. arcangeliana
6,0 $ Odour not of iodoform when drying: $ M. flavescens

